From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: v-zhangxiaomeng5 <v-zhangxiaomeng5@xiaomi.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Apr 2026 15:28:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] cxa_personality.cpp: fix _Unwind_State bitwise operation
 error on ARM GCC

On ARM, the C++ exception ABI (EHABI) defines _Unwind_State as an enum type. GCC 15 with -Werror rejects the implicit conversion from int back to _Unwind_State after a bitwise &= operation. Add static_cast to make the conversion explicit. This code is inside the _LIBCXXABI_ARM_EHABI branch and only affects ARM targets. Other architectures use the Itanium ABI where the equivalent parameter is int, so they are unaffected.

Signed-off-by: v-zhangxiaomeng5 <v-zhangxiaomeng5@xiaomi.com>
---
 src/cxa_personality.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/cxa_personality.cpp b/src/cxa_personality.cpp
index 5f6e75c..d72d3ef 100644
--- a/src/cxa_personality.cpp
+++ b/src/cxa_personality.cpp
@@ -1074,7 +1074,7 @@ __gxx_personality_v0(_Unwind_State state,
 
     // Check the undocumented force unwinding behavior
     bool is_force_unwinding = state & _US_FORCE_UNWIND;
-    state &= ~_US_FORCE_UNWIND;
+    state = static_cast<_Unwind_State>(state & ~_US_FORCE_UNWIND);
 
     scan_results results;
     switch (state) {
